{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams\/binarydecisiondiagram"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A shared table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams: Boolean functions of a fixed number"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of variables, each a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test one variable and branch to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"low child (the variable false) and a high child (true), down to the constants (Bryant,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“Graph-Based Algorithms for Boolean Function Manipulation”, 1986)."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BinaryDecisionDiagram"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Variables are tested in index order, 0 nearest the root. The table never holds two vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that test the same variable with the same children, nor a vertex whose children are equal, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each function has one vertex: two "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/Function","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" values are equal exactly when they are the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)          \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)              \/\/ 5","diagram.vertexCount(of: f)                            \/\/ 5: x0, x1, x2 and both constants","let g = diagram.restrict(f, variable: 2, to: false)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1","g == diagram.and(x0, x1)                              \/\/ true"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Functions are built by the mutating methods, which add vertices to the table and leave every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"existing function as it was; a function belongs to the table it was built in and its copies."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The table keeps every vertex it has made."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/ComputedTableStatistics-swift.struct","doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/Function","doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/GraphView-swift.struct","doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/Operator"],"title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/init(variableCount:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/computedTableStatistics-swif